// Drives the washout from the root boundary: a host writes the vehicle's
// KINEMATIC, gravity-free body acceleration into `ain`, its body angular rate
// into `win` and its body angular acceleration into `wdin`, all at the motion
// datum, and its attitude into `qin` as a quaternion, body to inertial. It
// reads the commanded platform motion at the datum back from `aout`, `vout`,
// `pout`. Not specific force -- a vehicle at rest drives `ain` with {0, 0, 0},
// level or on a slope, and the slope's share of gravity comes from `qin`; see
// the boundary note in `Classical.se` for why, and for the -2 g that reading
// it the other way round produces.
sim Washout {
    root: washout.Classical {};

    step:     1 (ms);
    solver:   rk4;
    duration: 2 (s);
}
